---
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InstagramEmbed from "../components/InstagramEmbed.astro";
import XiaoMaoStory from "../components/XiaoMaoStory.astro";
import { base } from "../lib/site";
---
<Layout
  title="赵郎溪 · xiao mao diao yu"
  description="Curious cats, ocean blues, and thoughts on technology, culture, and everything in between. Jade Zhao · 赵郎溪."
  canonical="https://zhao-langxi.github.io/zhao-langxi/"
  current="home"
  bodyClass="home"
  ogTitle="赵郎溪 · little cat fishing"
  ogDescription="A little corner of the internet for Chinese storytelling, personal reflections, and questions about what deserves attention."
>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header>
      <img
        class="hero-photo"
        src={`${base}assets/fishing.jpg`}
        alt="Jade Zhao on a boat, holding a fishing rod, open water behind her."
        width="960"
        height="540"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <p>赵郎溪 · @zhao.langxi</p>
      <h1>xiao mao diao yu</h1>
      <p class="home-tagline">
        Curious cats, ocean blues, and thoughts on technology, culture, and everything in between.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hi, I'm Jade! I'm an Informatics student at Indiana University who loves exploring the
        connections between technology, culture, and storytelling.
      </p>
      <p>
        One story I keep coming back to is <em lang="zh-Hans">小猫钓鱼</em> (The Little Cat Goes Fishing),
        a Chinese children's tale about a curious kitten learning the importance of focus and patience.
        As I have explored large language models and AI, I have found myself thinking about that
        lesson in a new way: how do we build systems that pay attention to what matters without
        getting lost in distractions?
      </p>
      <p>
        Zhao Langxi is my little corner of the internet for exploring questions like that, sharing
        personal reflections, and collecting the things that inspire me. Expect a little technology,
        a little Chinese storytelling, plenty of ocean blue, and, of course, cats.
      </p>
      <p class="section-kicker">
        Ships live on <a href="https://jadexzhao.github.io/jadexzhao/" rel="noopener noreferrer">jadexzhao</a>.
        Classroom notes live on
        <a href="https://matchaxmoxie.github.io/matchaxmoxie/" rel="noopener noreferrer">matchaxmoxie</a>.
        Days live on
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/zhao.langxi" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram @zhao.langxi</a>.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article>
      <XiaoMaoStory idPrefix="home" />
      <p class="xiaomao__more">
        Stay for the analogy:
        <a href={`${base}xiao-mao-diao-yu.html#llm`}>what this story can (and cannot) teach us about AI</a>.
      </p>

      <section id="name" aria-labelledby="name-heading">
        <h2 id="name-heading">The story behind my name · <span lang="zh-Hans">我的名字</span></h2>
        <p>
          The characters on this door are <strong lang="zh-Hans">赵郎溪</strong>.
          In pinyin that is <strong>Zhào Lángxī</strong> ... ordinary dictionary readings, not a
          family lecture I am inventing here.
        </p>
        <ul class="name-list">
          <li><span lang="zh-Hans">赵</span> · Zhào · the family surname.</li>
          <li><span lang="zh-Hans">郎溪</span> · Lángxī · the given name as written on this site.</li>
          <li>Jade Zhao is the English name I use. <span lang="zh-Hans">赵郎溪</span> is the name I wanted to grow into.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="placeholder-note">
          Why those two given-name characters were chosen, and any family story behind them, is
          still waiting for me to write it in my own words. I am not filling that gap with a pretty
          guess.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="story" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
        <h2 id="story-heading">How I got to the river</h2>
        <p>
          On Instagram the bio is still the true one: <em>xiao mao diao yu</em> ... little cat fishing ...
          <em>pov reformed ipad kid</em>. The fishing photo is not a brand exercise. It is me, on a boat,
          before anyone asked for a résumé line.
        </p>
        <p>
          I am Jade Zhao. Chinese American. I grew up in a family Chinese restaurant in central Indiana
          (Greenfield, Indiana). Mum drove Greenfield into Indianapolis so I could reach libraries, camps,
          and classrooms that did not exist on our street. A system either survives a real customer or it
          does not. That is still how I read a room.
        </p>
        <p>
          IU felt mutual. I came. The campus kept me. Sample Gates stopped being a postcard. Teter Hall,
          room 102, became the infinite sleepover ... new names in the group chat, a roommate who turns into
          your Sunday person, a squirrel winning against a peanut-butter jar. Then Bloomington stopped
          feeling like a place I was visiting.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="doors" aria-labelledby="doors-heading">
        <h2 id="doors-heading">Days already lived</h2>
        <ol class="essay-index">
          <li class="essay-index-item">
            <a href={`${base}iu.html`}>
              <span class="essay-kicker">Campus · Bloomington</span>
              <span class="essay-title">IU</span>
              <span class="essay-dek">Welcome Week, 900+ organisations, Little 500, IUDM, Sample Gates, and the ordinary Tuesdays in between.</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li class="essay-index-item">
            <a href={`${base}indiana.html`}>
              <span class="essay-kicker">College town · home weekends</span>
              <span class="essay-title">Indiana</span>
              <span class="essay-dek">Kirkwood, Lake Monroe, College Mall, and the drive home to the restaurant.</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li class="essay-index-item">
            <a href={`${base}spain.html`}>
              <span class="essay-kicker">Study abroad · Spring 2026</span>
              <span class="essay-title">Spain</span>
              <span class="essay-dek">Universidad Complutense de Madrid, then Segovia, Cáceres, Trujillo, Tenerife.</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li class="essay-index-item">
            <a href={`${base}days.html`}>
              <span class="essay-kicker">BeReal · the pictures</span>
              <span class="essay-title">Days</span>
              <span class="essay-dek">Fourteen frames from Downloads: campus, Kirkwood, Madrid sidewalks.</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section id="instagram" aria-labelledby="ig-heading">
        <h2 id="ig-heading">From Instagram @zhao.langxi</h2>
        <p>
          The live grid, not a recap. Memorial Stadium in a penguin onesie. Night game lights. Friends.
        </p>
        <div class="ig-grid">
          <InstagramEmbed
            href="https://www.instagram.com/p/De-VPhSltw0/"
            title="Memorial Stadium · penguin onesie"
          />
          <InstagramEmbed
            href="https://www.instagram.com/p/Dey2zHiFo0F/"
            title="A Tuesday with people I like"
          />
          <InstagramEmbed
            href="https://www.instagram.com/p/De5Z4fPlpze/"
            title="Memorial Stadium at night"
          />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="hiatus" aria-labelledby="hiatus-heading">
        <h2 id="hiatus-heading">Older essays, still here</h2>
        <p>
          Digital Humans and human-robot interaction pieces are parked, not deleted.
          If you came for ships and a résumé, that lives on
          <a href="https://jadexzhao.github.io/jadexzhao/" rel="noopener noreferrer">jadexzhao</a>.
        </p>
        <p><a href={`${base}archive.html`}>Writing archive</a></p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
